{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":21899301,"ns":0,"title":"Disquotational principle","extract":"The disquotational principle is a philosophical principle which holds that a rational speaker will accept \"p\" if and only if they believe p. The quotation marks indicate that the statement p is being treated as a sentence, and not as a proposition.","description":"Philosophical assertion about rational thought","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}